# Design for Snipfluent (SFL)
Visual design documentation and guidelines for the SFL application.

## Brand Identity
- **Name**: Snipfluent / SFL
- **Tagline**: "Audio snippets for being fluent in anyting"
- **Core values**: Accessibility, Simplicity, Engagement, Personalization

## Design Principles
- **Simple and familiar**: Follow established UI patterns that modern users already understand
- **Mobile-first**: Design for mobile screens first, then scale up to larger devices
- **Visual hierarchy**: Use size, color, and spacing to guide users through the interface
- **Icon-focused**: Prefer intuitive icons over excessive text where appropriate
- **Interactive feedback**: Use subtle animations to confirm user actions
- **Consistency**: Maintain coherent design patterns throughout the application

## Color Palette
- **Primary**: #1DB954 (Spotify Green)
- **Secondary**: #191414 (Spotify Black)
- **Accent**: #1ED760 (Bright Green for highlights)
- **Neutrals**:
  - Background: #121212 (Dark Grey)
  - Surface: #282828 (Medium Grey)
  - Text: #FFFFFF (White)
  - Subdued Text: #B3B3B3 (Light Grey)
- **Semantic**:
  - Success: #1DB954 (Green)
  - Error: #E61E32 (Red)
  - Warning: #FFCE00 (Yellow)
  - Info: #2E77D0 (Blue)

## Typography
- **Primary Font**: Inter (Sans-serif)
- **Headings**:
  - H1: 32px/40px, Bold
  - H2: 24px/32px, Bold
  - H3: 20px/28px, Semibold
  - H4: 18px/24px, Semibold
- **Body**:
  - Regular: 16px/24px
  - Small: 14px/20px
  - Caption: 12px/16px
- **Font Weights**:
  - Regular: 400
  - Medium: 500
  - Semibold: 600
  - Bold: 700

## Spacing System
- Base unit: 4px
- Common spacings: 4px, 8px, 12px, 16px, 24px, 32px, 48px, 64px
- Component padding: 16px
- Section margins: 24px

## Component Library
Using shadcn/ui as the foundation for our component library

### Core Components
- **Buttons**:
  - Primary: Filled green (#1DB954)
  - Secondary: Outlined white/green
  - Tertiary: Text only
  - Icon: Circle with icon centered
  - Sizes: Small (32px), Medium (40px), Large (48px)
- **Cards**:
  - Snippet Card: For displaying audio snippets
  - Topic Card: For displaying topic categories
  - Player Card: For the active playing audio
- **Input Controls**:
  - Text fields
  - Checkboxes
  - Radio buttons
  - Toggle switches
  - Sliders (for audio control)

### Navigation
- **Top Navigation Bar**:
  - Logo (left)
  - Page title (center)
  - User profile (right)
  - Back button when applicable (left)
- **Bottom Tab Bar** (mobile):
  - Home/Explore
  - Search
  - My Snippets
  - Create New
  - Profile
- **Sidebar** (desktop):
  - Collapsible
  - Same navigation items as bottom tab bar

## Web Application
### Global Elements
- **Header**:
  - Consistent across all pages
  - User profile dropdown with settings, logout options
  - Notification indicator
- **Footer**:
  - Links to Terms, Privacy, Support
  - Copyright information

### Page Layouts

#### Login/Authentication
- Clean, minimal layout
- Large logo centered
- Clear call-to-action
- **Components**:
  - Email/username input
  - Password input with show/hide toggle
  - "Remember me" checkbox
  - Login button (primary)
  - "Signup instead" link
  - OAuth buttons (Google, GitHub)
  - Forgot password link

#### Signup
- Stepped process with progress indicator
- **Components**:
  - Email validation
  - Password requirements feedback
  - Username availability check
  - First/Last name inputs
  - Terms acceptance checkbox
  - Submit button (disabled until all required fields valid)

#### Home/Explore
- Featured content at top (carousel)
- Category sections with horizontal scrolling
- **Components**:
  - Hero carousel (featured snippets)
  - Category headers with "see all" option
  - Snippet cards with:
    - Thumbnail/topic icon
    - Title
    - Duration
    - Topic tags
    - Play button overlay

#### Audio Listening
- Large focus on the currently playing audio
- **Components**:
  - Central visualization (animated based on audio)
  - Title and metadata display
  - Progress bar with elapsed/remaining time
  - Playback controls:
    - Play/Pause (primary)
    - Skip forward 15s
    - Skip backward 15s
    - Speed control (0.5x-2x)
  - Volume control
  - Transcript toggle with expandable bottom sheet
  - "Interrupt/Ask" button with microphone activation
  - Save/Favorite button
  - Share button

#### My Snippets
- Grid/List view toggle
- Sort and filter options
- **Components**:
  - Search bar for personal library
  - Filter dropdown (date, duration, topic)
  - Sort dropdown (newest, oldest, most played)
  - Snippet cards with:
    - Thumbnail
    - Title
    - Creation date
    - Duration
    - Quick play button
    - Options menu (rename, delete, share)

#### Create New Snippet
- Step-by-step wizard interface
- **Components**:
  - Topic selection (chips/tags)
  - Length/duration selector
  - Tone selector (professional, conversational, humorous)
  - Advanced options expander
  - Generate button
  - Progress indicator during generation
  - Preview option after generation

### Responsive Behavior
- **Mobile** (<768px):
  - Single column layout
  - Bottom navigation
  - Reduced padding
  - Stacked components
- **Tablet** (768px-1024px):
  - Two-column layouts where appropriate
  - Side navigation (collapsible)
  - Increased whitespace
- **Desktop** (>1024px):
  - Multi-column layouts
  - Fixed side navigation
  - Maximum content width (1200px)
  - Increased padding and margins

## Microinteractions and Animation
- **Audio Visualization**:
  - Waveform animation synchronized with audio playback
  - Soft pulsing effect when speaking
- **Transitions**:
  - Page transitions: Fade (200ms)
  - Component mounting: Slight scale + fade (150ms)
  - List items: Staggered entrance (50ms delay between items)
- **Feedback**:
  - Button press: Slight scale down + color change
  - Success actions: Green check mark animation
  - Error feedback: Subtle shake animation

## Accessibility
- **Color Contrast**:
  - All text meets WCAG AA standards (4.5:1 for normal text, 3:1 for large text)
  - Interactive elements have sufficient contrast against backgrounds
- **Screen Readers**:
  - All images have alt text
  - ARIA labels for all interactive elements
  - Proper heading hierarchy
- **Keyboard Navigation**:
  - Logical tab order
  - Focus indicators visible and consistent
- **Additional Considerations**:
  - Transcript available for all audio content
  - Adjustable playback speed
  - Captions support

## File Structure and Assets
- **Image Assets**:
  - Icons: SVG format
  - Logos: SVG and PNG (@1x, @2x, @3x)
  - Thumbnails: WebP format
- **Design Files**:
  - Component library in Figma
  - Prototype links for key user flows
  - Design tokens exported for development

